  "body": "Source-scoped theory + actual Rust implementation, original rei_bianchi source commit f7830e2f55e7a1938bc3c98f61b60651f8dae474. Parent BASS_HE HE19 PR65 at 8e759508317f5ffbc891c5876ff10771ad79297b; new HEAD ccd9125e6776f3f8d3388d70c6675873464c5f30.\n\nConstructive result: exact non-tilted LRS Killing-energy factor and all three H/He photo-threshold preimage splits of the original BB50K Simpson32 spectral bins, retaining positive child supports and original source photon N/U, with radiation redshift work and no false permanent passive removal. Direct native Rust `Driver`, `AxbiSource`, `CovariantPhoton` used, no original owner code changed. New original-crate-link tests 4/4 PASS. Independently rebuilt original C8 native source-only runner, 20/20 original boundary fractions identical to original fixture (max difference 0).\n\nNCP: 72 distinct q(-.005,0,+.005) \u00d7 m(4,8,16,32,64,128) \u00d7 source steps(1,8,32,128); 2 serial + 2 parallel repeats = **288 real Rust executions**, all scientific outputs identical. Largest normalized source N 9.43e-15, U 7.92e-15, total redshift work 4.30e-14; no threshold-straddling children. q=0 m16 n128: old source-grid boundary 0.03288561876450831, actual reconstructed continuous-source UV cutoff crossing 8.420882174665324e-05, ratio 390.5246. This is NOT an ionization/CMB error ratio. 16-process walls .327/.335s vs serial 2.892/2.775s; 32-process .317s, 64-process .338s in single additional same-science runs. Scoped source-only process throughput, not production EoR speedup.\n\nFiles: research/he20_native_md14_20261015/README_KO.md, src/native_md14_cut.rs, src/run_native.py, results/RESULT_STATUS.json, results/HE20_NATIVE_72_CASES.csv, original Rust C8 replay and Rust unit test log. Native original rlib compiled Rust1.99.0, source provenance preserved. Next science gate: actual coupled original Grackle Case-A H/He photoabsorption/recombination/thermal A/B and energy\u00d7time refinement before EoR/observer claims. Warm HE18 source not mixed with cold MD14. Keep this PR draft and unmerged. A source-restorable archive and Git bundle are being backed up to both private clouds with independent SHA readback.",
